% A rule base with a facts background (docs/user/reference/language.md §14.5).
% The two background programs are used only to read facts from a text:
% "Write it in English" offers their templates, and their rules add the
% facts of this program that follow (le_background.pl). This program never
% reasons with them: its queries answer as if the section were not there.
%
% The fabric construction has one value (it is declared in `the functions
% are:`): a construction that the text states beats one that a background
% derives, and two derived constructions that differ are a question.
%
% The two readings (§17.5): the strict reading admits the listing and the
% bridges of the garments background; the full reading also admits the
% customs presumptions.

the target language is: prolog.

the facts background includes these resources:
    background/garments, background/presumptions.

the functions are:
    the fabric construction of *a garment* is *a construction*; undefined.

the templates are:
    the kind of *a good* is *a kind*; undefined.
    the fabric of *a garment* is lightweight; undefined.
    the heading of *a good* is *a heading*.
    *a good* is classified in *a heading* by *a reading*.

the knowledge base mini tariff includes:

the heading of a good is 6109
    if the kind of the good is T-shirt
    and the fabric construction of the good is knitted
    and the fabric of the good is lightweight.

the heading of a good is 6205
    if the kind of the good is shirt
    and the fabric construction of the good is woven.

a good is classified in a heading by a reading
    if the reading is in [strict reading, full reading]
    and the heading of the good is the heading
        according to the reading.

the listing is admissible under strict reading.
the listing is admissible under full reading.
garments background is admissible under strict reading.
garments background is admissible under full reading.
customs presumptions is admissible under full reading.

scenario stated is, as stated in the listing:
    the kind of item one is T-shirt.
    the fabric construction of item one is knitted.
    the fabric of item one is lightweight.
    headings expects answers ["the heading of item one is 6109"].

scenario read is, as stated in the listing:
    the kind of item one is T-shirt, according to garments background, because "kind_by_name", confer "Men Tee Shirt".
    the fabric construction of item one is knitted, according to garments background, because "construction_by_field", confer "Craft of Weaving: Knit".
    the fabric of item one is lightweight, according to customs presumptions, because "tshirt_fabric", confer "Men Tee Shirt".
    readings expects answers ["item one is classified in 6109 by full reading"].

query headings is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query readings is:
    which good is classified in which heading by which reading.
